{
  "id": "crouzon-syndrome",
  "term": "Crouzon syndrome",
  "definition": "Crouzon syndrome is an inherited biological condition in which some skull bones fuse too early, typically leading to a short, broad head shape along with underdevelopment of the upper jaw and prominent eyes. It can also be associated with problems such as sleep apnea, hydrocephalus, and negative psychosocial effects.",
